# zarrow performance plan, round 3 (base eb10135)

Scratchpad = `C:\Users\cable\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\C--Users-cable-Documents-dev-zarrow--claude-worktrees-zig-0-17-migration-branch-f92e21\3ab19c71-6c26-4cbd-ba49-bd6ba48132fc\scratchpad`
(called `$S` below).

Every change below is already prototyped, tested and measured in a scratch copy of eb10135 (`$S\r4`). The
reference implementation is `$S\perf3.patch` (library + 4 new tests, 9 files, LF). `$S\perf3_harness.patch`
holds the optional benchmark-harness changes (item 8; needs a yes from the user). Both apply cleanly:

```sh
# repo files are CRLF on disk, the patches are LF: normalize the touched files first (autocrlf=input, so git status stays clean)
F="src/array/array_data.zig src/array/primitive_array.zig src/bitmap.zig src/buffer.zig src/compute/datum_permutation.zig src/compute/test_datum.zig src/concat_array_refs.zig src/ipc/stream_reader.zig src/ipc/stream_writer.zig"
sed -i 's/\r$//' $F && git apply $S/perf3.patch
# optional, item 8 only:
sed -i 's/\r$//' benchmarks/take_benchmark.zig benchmarks/primitive_builder_benchmark.zig benchmarks/ipc_roundtrip_benchmark.zig benchmarks/ipc_compressed_benchmark.zig && git apply $S/perf3_harness.patch
```
Verified on the patched tree: `zig build test` 360/360 (base 356 + 4 new) on 0.17 and on 0.16
(`--cache-dir .zig-cache16`), 0.16 `zig fmt --check` clean on all changed files, `zig build`, `zig build fuzz-corpus`
(14/14), `zig build examples` ok. Benchmark checksums identical to base on every benchmark.

The implementer may either apply the patch or type each item below in order; the code blocks below are the
patch's content (complete functions where a function is rewritten).

## 0. Measurement method and results

The machine has a long-running background load (a python3.13 process), so sequential runs drift by up to 2x.
All numbers here come from `$S\ab.sh A B N bench...`: it builds both trees (ReleaseFast, `-j2`, installs the
benchmark exes) and runs A,B,A,B,... N times, reporting min and median. Use it for every before/after claim.
Probes used for root causes: `$S\r4\benchmarks\p3_benchmark.zig` (builder/take/filter/concat breakdowns, three
allocators) and `p3ipc_benchmark.zig` (IPC write/read/zero-copy floors, raw libzstd floors). rdtsc phase
timers were added temporarily for filter and concat (not in the patch).

Final interleaved A/B, Zig 0.17, ns/row (base eb10135 -> perf3.patch; "+harness" = item 8 on top):

| Benchmark | base min/med | after min/med | +harness | arrow-rs | C++ | target |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| primitive_builder | 2.58 / 2.64 | 1.36 / 1.39 | 1.38 | 1.4 | - | <=1.5 yes |
| concat 12,500 x 16 | 9.08 / 9.42 | 4.13 / 4.42 | - | 5.8 | - | <=6 yes |
| filter string 50% | 5.18 / 5.39 | 2.46 / 2.48 | - | 2.6 | 2.0 | <=2.5 at the edge |
| take int32 nullable | 4.97 / 5.40 | 1.82 / 1.88 | 1.65 | 1.7 | 2.4 | <=2 yes |
| IPC zstd write+read | 28.5 / 29.4 | 27.2 / 28.6 | 26.2 | 45 | 21 | <=21 no (libzstd floor 21.3) |
| IPC write uncompressed | 3.06 / 3.40 | 3.03 / 3.88 | 0.47 | 3.0 | 2.1 | <=2.2 only with item 8 |
| IPC read copying | 4.59 / 5.34 | 1.02 / 1.51 | 0.87 | 2.2 | - | <=2.5 yes |
| IPC read zero-copy | 0.34 / 0.40 | 0.11 / 0.16 | 0.10 | - | 0.17 | <=0.2 yes |

Zig 0.16 A/B (5 runs): builder 2.96 -> 1.68, concat 9.25 -> 4.61, filter 5.33 -> 2.59, take 5.29 -> 1.74,
zstd 29.4 -> 27.9, write 2.93 -> 2.94, read 3.90 -> 0.89, zero-copy 0.33 -> 0.10.

## 1. Hand-off order (gain / risk)

| # | Item | Rows | Files | Gain | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Vectorized offsets validation | zero-copy read (also concat, every validateLayout) | array_data.zig | 3.3x | low, trust boundary kept |
| 2 | finishReset pre-sizes the next batch | primitive_builder | primitive_array.zig | 1.9x | low |
| 3 | Dense, branch-free take kernels | take | datum_permutation.zig | 2.9x | low-medium |
| 4 | Filter with dense u32 selections | filter | datum_permutation.zig (needs 3) | 2.2x | low |
| 5 | Reader reuses released bodies (SharedBuffer.reclaim) | IPC read copying (also multi-batch zstd) | buffer.zig, stream_reader.zig | 4.5x | medium, trust boundary |
| 6 | Two-pass N-ary concat | concat | concat_array_refs.zig, bitmap.zig | 2.2x | medium |
| 7 | Writer compresses straight into the final buffer | IPC zstd write | stream_writer.zig | about 0.2-0.5 ns | low, optional |
| 8 | Harness parity (smp allocator, reused sink) | IPC write, take, builder | benchmarks/*.zig | write 6x (harness only) | needs sign-off |

