### Item 1. Vectorized offsets validation (row: IPC read zero-copy 0.38 -> 0.10)

**Root cause (measured).** Zero-copy read of one 20k-row batch costs 6.8 us. Ablation: with the offsets
monotonicity check disabled it costs 0.8 us (0.039 ns/row), so 85% of zero-copy read is
`ArrayData.validateOffsetsI32` on the 20k string offsets. Its loop
`if (cur < prev or cur < 0) return error.InvalidOffsets;` exits early, so LLVM keeps it scalar (0.29 ns per offset,
probe `concat_validate_string_out` on 200k offsets). Arrow C++ gets 0.17 by not scanning offsets on read at all
(see section 3); we keep the full check and make it vector-speed.

**Change.** `src/array/array_data.zig`, inside `pub const ArrayData = struct`, add before `validateOffsetsI32`:
```zig
    /// True when `xs[k] <= xs[k + 1]` for every k. No early exit, so the compare-and-OR loop
    /// vectorizes; a hostile buffer costs the same as a valid one.
    fn isNonDecreasing(comptime T: type, xs: []const T) bool {
        if (xs.len < 2) return true;
        const L = 16;
        var bad: @Vector(L, u1) = @splat(0);
        var i: usize = 0;
        while (i + L < xs.len) : (i += L) {
            const a: @Vector(L, T) = xs[i..][0..L].*;
            const b: @Vector(L, T) = xs[i + 1 ..][0..L].*;
            bad |= @intFromBool(b < a);
        }
        var tail: u1 = 0;
        while (i + 1 < xs.len) : (i += 1) tail |= @intFromBool(xs[i + 1] < xs[i]);
        return @reduce(.Or, bad) == 0 and tail == 0;
    }
```
In both `validateOffsetsI32` and `validateOffsetsI64`, replace everything from `var prev: i32 = offsets[start];`
(resp. `i64`) to the end of the function body with (use `i64` in the I64 version):
```zig
        // Non-decreasing from a non-negative first offset implies every offset is >= 0.
        if (offsets[start] < 0) return error.InvalidOffsets;
        if (!isNonDecreasing(i32, offsets[start..needed_len])) return error.InvalidOffsets;
        const last = std.math.cast(usize, offsets[needed_len - 1]) orelse return error.InvalidOffsets;
        if (last > data_len) return error.InvalidOffsets;
```
The accepted set is unchanged (first >= 0, every step non-decreasing, last <= data_len). `@Vector` lowers to
AVX2 on x86_64 and to 4 NEON ops per step on aarch64; no inline asm. Variants measured and rejected: the same
loop with `bad = bad or (b < a)` (short-circuit, 0.23 ns/row) and with a `u8` accumulator (0.19); the explicit
16-lane vector gives 0.041 ns per offset.

**Trust boundary.** This runs on every IPC read, C-data import and `RecordBatch.init`. Same predicate, no early
exit, constant time per offset.

**Tests.** Existing: ~10 `validateLayout ... InvalidOffsets` tests in array_data.zig (all short arrays, so they only
reach the scalar tail). New (in the patch, end of array_data.zig):
`test "array data validateLayout finds a decreasing offset in the vector body and the tail"`: 41 increasing
offsets pass; a decrease at index 5 and 20 (vector body) and 39 (tail) each give `error.InvalidOffsets`.

**Expected.** Zero-copy read 0.33 -> 0.10 ns/row (measured 0.10-0.12). `validateLayout` on 200k string offsets
0.29 -> 0.04 ns/row, which also helps concat and every RecordBatch.init.

