```
- `decodeRecordBatchBody` gets a last parameter `spare: ?*?array_data.SharedBuffer`; replace
  `buffer.OwnedBuffer.initUninit(allocator, cursor)` with `reuseOrAlloc(allocator, spare, cursor)` and the return with
```zig
    const decoded_body = try owned.toShared(cursor);
    keepSpare(spare, decoded_body);
    return .{ .body = decoded_body, .buffers_meta = decoded_meta, .owned_body = true, .owned_meta = true };
```
- `buildRecordBatchFromFlatbuf` gets a last parameter `spare_decoded: ?*?array_data.SharedBuffer` and passes it to
  `decodeRecordBatchBody`. Callers: `nextRecordBatch` passes `&self.spare_decoded`;
  `buildRecordBatchFromMessageMetadata` passes `null`; `ingestDictionaryBatchWithMap` and the lz4 test call
  `decodeRecordBatchBody(..., null)`. FileReader is untouched (it reaches the decoder through
  `buildRecordBatchFromMessageMetadata`, so it keeps allocating).

**Trust boundary (flagged).** This is the untrusted-bytes path. All validation is unchanged and still happens
before or independent of reuse: `body_len` from the verified envelope, `readSliceAll` of exactly `body_len`
(short stream -> error, buffer freed by the errdefer), `layoutDecodedBody` caps declared sizes at
`max_decompressed_body_bytes` before `reuseOrAlloc` is called, `decompressZstdInto` / lz4 still require the exact
declared length, padding slots are still zeroed by the decoder, `validateLayout` on every column. A reused buffer
is only written when its ref count is 1, i.e. no batch, column slice or caller handle can observe the overwrite.
Bytes past `body_len` / `cursor` in a reused allocation hold old data but are outside every `SharedBuffer`
window and never reach the API or the writer.
Memory: a reader keeps at most two extra allocations (each within 2x of the last body) until the next message
or `deinit`.

**Tests.** Existing: all stream/file reader tests, pyarrow multi-batch fixtures, compressed roundtrip tests,
`expectZeroCopyMatchesCopy`. New (in the patch): `buffer.zig` "shared buffer reclaim returns the allocation only to
the last handle" (null while a second handle exists, the allocation after release, null for borrowed);
