### Item 6. Two-pass N-ary concat (row: concat 11.6 -> 4.2)

**Root cause (measured, rdtsc phases + ablations, cycles per row, both arrays).** Base `concatManyFlat` walked the
12,500 parts four times per array (type check in `concatArrayRefs`, sizing with a per-part popcount
`nullCountForArray`, `concatValidityMany`, values; strings a fifth for `concatManyBinary`'s own sizing). Each part
is a separate heap node (about 250 B with inline buffers, 3 MB of nodes per array), so every pass costs cache
misses. Ablations on the prototype: replacing `dataTypeEql(d.data_type, dt)` by a tag compare alone took concat
from 6.2 to 4.3 ns/row: copying each part's `DataType` union by value touches a second cache line of every node.
Skipping validity copy saved 7 of 28 cycles/row: `copyBits` on a 16-bit byte-aligned chunk called `@memcpy(2 bytes)`
per part. Per-part `@memcpy` of 64 B (int) / about 116 B (string) were calls too. About 9-10 cycles/row
(2.4 ns) is first-touch faults of the fresh 2.8 MB of outputs (probe `alloc+touch outputs`), which arrow-rs pays too.

**Change.**
(a) `src/bitmap.zig`, `copyBits`: replace the `if (full > 0) { ... }` block and add `byteAtBit` after the function:
```zig
