5. Arrow C++ / pyarrow `ipc.open_stream` does not run full validation (no offset monotonicity scan) by default; that is
   most of its 0.17 ns/row zero-copy lead. zarrow keeps the scan and is now at 0.10.

Where arrow-rs validates MORE than zarrow (follow-up hardening, not part of this perf round): its IPC read calls
`validate_data`, which (a) recounts nulls and rejects a FieldNode `null_count` that disagrees with the bitmap
(zarrow only checks `null_count <= length`; a lying count can make kernels that trust `null_count == 0` emit
"all valid"), and (b) UTF-8-validates `Utf8`/`LargeUtf8` values (zarrow does not). (a) costs one popcount per
column (about 0.02 ns/row); suggested place: `readArrayFromMeta` before `validateLayout`.

