### Item 2. finishReset pre-sizes the next batch (row: primitive_builder 2.7 -> 1.4)

**Root cause (measured).** `finish()` hands `values` to the array (`toShared` empties it), so every batch after
the first starts at capacity 0 and regrows 64 B -> 800 KB: about 14 `OwnedBuffer.resize` calls, each a
PageAllocator realloc (new mapping + copy) plus a memset of the new half plus first-touch page faults. Probes,
200k rows x 80: `builder` 2.74-2.85, `builder_reserved` (same appends after `reserve(rows)`) 1.41-1.46,
`grow_realloc_zero` (just the doubling pattern) 1.7-1.9. The per-append path already matches arrow-rs (1.4 ns
including arrow-rs's own Vec growth from 0, which reallocs without zeroing). Allocator does not matter
(page vs smp within 2%).

**Change.** `src/array/array/primitive_array.zig` is wrong path; the file is `src/array/primitive_array.zig`,
`PrimitiveBuilder(...).finishReset`:
```zig
        pub fn finishReset(self: *Self) !ArrayRef {
            const finished_len = self.len;
            const finished_ref = try self.finish();
            try self.reset();
            // Batches built in a loop are usually the same size: start the next one at that capacity
            // (one allocation instead of ~log2(len) regrowths). On OOM it just grows lazily.
            if (finished_len > 0) {
                if (OwnedBuffer.init(self.allocator, finished_len * @sizeOf(T))) |buf| self.values = buf else |_| {}
            }
            return finished_ref;
        }
```
`OwnedBuffer.init` (zeroed) on purpose: `appendNull` does not write the value slot, so null slots rely on zeroed
memory; `initUninit` here would leak old heap bytes into null slots (and into IPC output). Validity is unchanged
(still allocated lazily on the first null). Do not touch `finish()` / `reset()`; other builders keep their
behavior (only PrimitiveBuilder is hot in the benchmark; same one-liner can be copied to BooleanBuilder /
BinaryBuilder later if they show up).

**Tests.** Existing: "primitive builder appends values and nulls", "duration builder alias keeps unit across
finishReset reuse" (array.zig), struct/record-batch builder tests. No boundary change; no new test needed
(behavior identical, only capacity). Optional one-liner check if desired: after `finishReset` of 3 rows,
`builder.values.len() >= 3 * @sizeOf(i32)`.

**Expected.** 2.7 -> 1.4 ns/row (measured 1.36-1.46 on 0.17, 1.68 on 0.16).

