### Item 5. Reader reuses released bodies (row: IPC read copying 4.7 -> 1.0)

**Root cause (measured).** `readMessageOptional` allocates a fresh `OwnedBuffer.initUninit(body_len)` per message
(470 KB per batch here) and `readSliceAll`s into it. Fresh pages fault on first touch: the floor "fresh alloc +
memcpy per batch" alone is 4.6 ns/row with smp_allocator and 0.44 with a page-retaining arena (probe
`rt_read_floor_alloc_memcpy_*`); the full copying read is 4.35 (smp) vs 0.82 (arena). So the read cost is the
allocator handing back fresh pages, not zarrow's decode. arrow-rs/C++ reuse heap pages (Windows heap /
mimalloc). Fix in the shared place: when the caller has released the previous batch, the body allocation has no
other handle left and can be refilled.

**Change.**
(a) `src/buffer.zig`, `SharedBuffer`, after `isEmpty`:
```zig
    /// Turns the last handle to an `OwnedBuffer` allocation back into a writable `OwnedBuffer`
    /// (full capacity, contents unspecified) and empties this handle. Returns null, leaving the
    /// handle untouched, when other handles exist or the memory is not OwnedBuffer-allocated.
    /// Like arrow-rs `Buffer::into_mutable`.
    pub fn reclaim(self: *Self) ?OwnedBuffer {
        const storage = self.storage orelse return null;
        if (storage.release_fn != &BufferStorage.releaseDefault) return null;
        if (storage.ref_count.load(.acquire) != 1) return null;
        self.* = empty;
        return .{ .data = @alignCast(storage.data[ALIGNMENT..]), .allocator = storage.allocator };
    }
```
(b) `src/ipc/stream_reader.zig`:
- `StreamReader` fields after `source`:
```zig
    /// Extra handles on the last copied body and the last decoded (decompressed) body. Once the
    /// caller drops every batch that used one, the next message reuses that allocation instead
    /// of faulting in fresh pages; otherwise the handle is released and a new buffer allocated.
    spare_body: ?array_data.SharedBuffer = null,
    spare_decoded: ?array_data.SharedBuffer = null,
```
- `deinit`: after the `source` release add
  `if (self.spare_body) |*b| b.release(); self.spare_body = null;` and the same for `spare_decoded`.
- New free functions before `fn readMessageOptional`:
```zig
/// A writable buffer of at least `len` bytes: the allocation held in `spare` when no batch uses
/// it any more, else a fresh one. `spare == null` always allocates.
fn reuseOrAlloc(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, spare: ?*?array_data.SharedBuffer, len: usize) error{OutOfMemory}!OwnedBuffer {
    if (spare) |slot| if (slot.*) |*old| {
        if (old.reclaim()) |reclaimed| {
            slot.* = null;
            // Within 2x so one huge body is not pinned by a stream of small batches.
            if (reclaimed.len() >= len and reclaimed.len() / 2 <= len) return reclaimed;
            var unfit = reclaimed;
            unfit.deinit();
        } else {
            old.release();
            slot.* = null;
        }
    };
    return OwnedBuffer.initUninit(allocator, len);
}

/// Keeps one extra handle on `buf` in `spare` (replacing the previous one) for `reuseOrAlloc`.
fn keepSpare(spare: ?*?array_data.SharedBuffer, buf: array_data.SharedBuffer) void {
    const slot = spare orelse return;
    if (slot.*) |*old| old.release();
    slot.* = buf.retain();
}
```
